# EXPECT: defined inside a loop body and referenced by name outside that loop
# ouroboros#194 sibling: a define inside a `for` body is loop-scoped on the
# VM -- the post-loop `inner of 100` dies "undefined variable 'inner'" -- but
# the lifted C function is module-wide and would answer 139. Refused by
# name. The VM runs the program up to that death (prints nothing before it
# because the death is inside f); the refuse tier needs a VM rc 0 program,
# so the escaping reference sits in a branch the VM does not take.
define f(q) as:
    local acc is 0
    for x in [1, 2, 3]:
        define inner(d) as:
            return x + d
        acc is acc + (inner of 10)
    if q == 99:
        acc is acc + (inner of 100)
    return acc
print of (f of 1)
